# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
#
# The root configuration, minus one thing that is Catch2's rather than ours.
#
# Every TEST_CASE expands to a static registrar object whose constructor registers the test
# with the framework, and that constructor can throw. bugprone-throwing-static-initialization
# is right about it and there is nothing to do: it is how Catch2 finds tests, and it fires
# once per test case -- eighty-one times across this directory as it stands.
#
# Scoped to tests/ rather than turned off at the root, because the check is a good one
# everywhere else: a global initialised from something that can throw really is a program
# that dies before main with no way to say why.

InheritParentConfig: true

Checks: >
  -bugprone-throwing-static-initialization,
  -cert-err58-cpp,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange

# The third one is also Catch2's, and it needs naming here rather than filtering out by
# path: the static analyser's diagnostics do not go through HeaderFilterRegex or
# ExcludeHeaderFilterRegex, so a finding inside catch_result_type.hpp arrives whatever
# those say. Checked by passing --exclude-header-filter explicitly, which changed nothing.
